# Everything not needed to build. Two reasons this is aggressive:
#
#   1. Build context size. Sending .venv/ and .git/ to the daemon adds seconds
#      to every build and invalidates the cache on every branch switch.
#   2. Secrets. A .env or a .pem copied into a layer stays in the image
#      history even if a later layer deletes it.

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
.DS_Store
